From 43ac1cebfdeac0160a77101cb58395adfbd8c377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:50:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: fix CSIPHY4 endpoint lane numbering and add mandatory
 clock-lanes

The camss-side endpoint used the sensor's 1-based CSI-2 lane numbering
and omitted clock-lanes entirely:

	csiphy4_front_ep: endpoint {
		data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
		remote-endpoint = <&camf_imx471_ep>;
	};

Both are wrong for camss. Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/
qcom,sm8250-camss.yaml lists clock-lanes AND data-lanes under "required"
for each port, and the CSIPHY side numbers lanes from 0. The other
SM8250 board in tree that enables camss, sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi,
writes its ports as:

	csiphy4_ep: endpoint {
		clock-lanes = <7>;
		data-lanes = <0 1>;
		bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
	};

Consequence of the 1-based numbering, from patch 0087's diagnostic:

  CSIPHY DIAG(0087): id=4 link_freq=200000000 timer_clk=300000000
                     settle_cnt=24 lane_mask=0x9e num_data=4
  CSIPHY DIAG(0087):   data lane 0 -> pos 1
  CSIPHY DIAG(0087):   data lane 1 -> pos 2
  CSIPHY DIAG(0087):   data lane 2 -> pos 3
  CSIPHY DIAG(0087):   data lane 3 -> pos 4

csiphy_lanes_enable() builds CTRL5 as BIT(pos * 2) over those positions,
giving BIT(2) | BIT(4) | BIT(6) | BIT(8) = 0x154 instead of the correct
BIT(0) | BIT(2) | BIT(4) | BIT(6) = 0x55. Physical lane 0 was therefore
never enabled while bits for lane slots that do not exist were set. The
PHY cannot lock on a link whose first data lane is switched off, which
is why every ioctl succeeded, the media graph linked, VIDIOC_STREAMON
was accepted, and DQBUF then blocked forever with no error and no CSIPHY
interrupt.

link_freq and settle_cnt were already correct (200000000 and 24), so
timing was never the problem -- only the lane mapping.

The sensor endpoint is deliberately left at data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>. That
side uses the standard 1-based CSI-2 convention, and imx471_check_hwcfg()
rejects anything other than 4 data lanes.

Also pull in dt-bindings/media/video-interfaces.h for
MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY.
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts    | 29 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
index be285890a..a67df44ad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-kebab.dts
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/media/video-interfaces.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/arm/qcom,ids.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/regulator/qcom,rpmh-regulator.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/phy/phy.h>
@@ -2043,7 +2044,33 @@ ports {
 		port@4 {
 			reg = <4>;
 			csiphy4_front_ep: endpoint {
-				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
+				/*
+				 * CSIPHY-side lane numbering is 0-based and
+				 * clock-lanes is mandatory -- see
+				 * Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/
+				 * qcom,sm8250-camss.yaml, which lists both
+				 * clock-lanes and data-lanes under "required",
+				 * and sm8250-xiaomi-elish-common.dtsi, the other
+				 * SM8250 board that enables camss.
+				 *
+				 * This endpoint previously carried the sensor-side
+				 * 1-based numbering, data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>, and no
+				 * clock-lanes at all. csiphy_lanes_enable() then
+				 * programmed CTRL5 as BIT(pos * 2) over positions
+				 * 1..4 -- BIT(2,4,6,8) = 0x154 -- instead of
+				 * positions 0..3 -- BIT(0,2,4,6) = 0x55. Physical
+				 * lane 0 was left disabled and nonexistent lane
+				 * slots were enabled, so the PHY never locked.
+				 * Confirmed live by patch 0087's diagnostic:
+				 *   lane_mask=0x9e, data lanes at pos 1,2,3,4
+				 *
+				 * The sensor endpoint keeps <1 2 3 4>: that side is
+				 * the standard 1-based CSI-2 convention and the
+				 * imx471 driver requires exactly 4 data lanes.
+				 */
+				clock-lanes = <7>;
+				data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+				bus-type = <MEDIA_BUS_TYPE_CSI2_DPHY>;
 				remote-endpoint = <&camf_imx471_ep>;
 			};
 		};
-- 
2.55.0

